worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_formalization_targets.js"
  ceiling 463
  rationale "Issue #1186 R5 deformalization from every rendered target, browser twin of rust/src/solver_handlers/formalization_task_targets.rs. The Lean 4 and Rocq renderings are matched against the clause and atom templates of data/seed/formal-targets.lino run in reverse, and the Links Notation rendering is read field by field with field names taken from the same templates; no target surface is spelled in the module. Added 2026-10-07. Ceiling moved 289 to 379 for issue #1186 R4/R6 (2026-10-07): formalRmlSource, the browser twin of rml_source in rust/src/solver_handlers/formalization_task_rml.rs, renders the clause as the typed fragment rml export lean reads from the export_target rml templates of data/seed/formal-targets.lino, and formalRmlCheck states that the browser never runs it. Ceiling moved 379 to 463 for issue #1186 R4 (2026-10-08): formalProverRecords, formalProverUnit and formalProverChecks, the browser twin of rust/src/solver_handlers/formalization_task_prover.rs, build each prover record's compile unit from data/seed/formal-targets.lino and render the localized prover status through the formalAiProverHost seam the JavaScript server installs (js/server/prover-host.mjs); the browser installs none, so its provers are absent."
